A||||6||Boo||rad fan
Z||000000||Boo||07-22-99||01:03 PM||||Help!!  I have a 84 4cyl 4sp and the rad fan is shot...apparently I am sol as there were not too many with a/c.  My mechanic is trying to find me the whole housing as the resister is pooched also...Is there an alternative here...does anybody know...he powered up the fan somehow, and it is pooched also...just found this site (looking for a new car)and thought I would give it a shot...any help would be greatly appreciated...I really dont want to have to buy a new car...
Z||000001||theogre||07-22-99||01:15 PM||||you have the 2 speed fan, which is fairly rare. All fiero's have a fan, but only some 4 cyl's had the 2 speed unit. <p>you could, in a pinch, put a single speed fan in and connect it's + lead to the both the + leads from the spedd harness. That way the temp switch, and AC control, can activate it as need be. The best way to do this is cut the connector off the old fan. That way if you find a replacement for the 2 speed you can later just plug it back in.
Z||000002||Boo||07-22-99||02:13 PM||||thanks for the info just one (or two ?'s more) My mechanic mentioned something about the replacement motor which he can get has a different pitch to it..(or the fan its self)will this affect the cooling process of the motor..i dont care about the a/c  or am i just talking nonsense...
Z||000003||theogre||07-23-99||07:44 AM||||increased pitch would increase airflow some. lowered pitch would drop the flow some. Plus the single speed fan will run at full speed when the 2 speed would have been on low..... so you'll flow more air anyway.<p>It probably won't make to much diferance unless the pitch change is large. The fan is there mainly for lowspeed, or stoped, traffic. It can help even at highway speeds, but how much depends on a few things, like exactly what nose is on the car.
Z||000004||Boo||07-23-99||03:21 PM||||im feeling much better about this whole thing...it has the original nose as in the more angled one as opposed to the rounded nose. Now should I get a new thermostat ( ie.one that kicks fan in at lower temp) or should the original one be ok...thanks again
Z||000005||theogre||07-23-99||07:32 PM||||the 2 speed fan low comes on at around 217. thats probably as low as you need for most things. If you tie both the low, and high, speed leads like I said above, that's when it will turn on from heat. The AC will also turn it on regardless of engine heat.<br>
Z||000006||Boo||07-29-99||04:52 PM||||Thanks for all your help...i am back up and running finally...feels good to be behind the wheel again...
